# N3 example: fibonacci.
# Companion to fibonacci.pl: a backward-chained recursive definition,
# mirroring hanoi.n3's style.
#
# Adapted: fibonacci.pl asks fib(100, ?value), computed efficiently only
# because the tabled evaluator memoizes repeated fib(?n, ?) calls.
# eyeron's N3 backward resolution is not tabled the same way and instead
# has a fixed recursion-depth safety limit (32); fib(100)'s call chain is
# ~99 deep, so this asks fib(30, ?value) instead, well within that limit.

@prefix math: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/math#>.
@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/eyepl/examples/fibonacci#>.

{(0) :fib 0} <= true.
{(1) :fib 1} <= true.

{(?n) :fib ?f} <= {
    ?n math:greaterThan 1.
    (?n 1) math:difference ?previous.
    (?n 2) math:difference ?earlier.
    (?previous) :fib ?a.
    (?earlier) :fib ?b.
    (?a ?b) math:sum ?f.
}.

{(30) :fib ?value} => {:query :fib ?value}.
